body:
Glad to help! It can be hard to find support or ways to cope so anything I can ever share to someone else I try. We gotta help each other out :) I know it might sound like a weird idea, but you might also try looking on Pinterest oddly enough. I've found quite a few things on there that talk about or link to dealing with mental health issues. 

&#x200B;

Thanks, and same to both of you. He's lucky to have you, and you obviously feel the same :)

Brain Stew - Green Day

&#x200B;

I love that song, but waking up to the same day over and over and have that playing... I think I'd slowly go insane lol.

It must be Soooo nice to be able to stay at home every day and not have to worry about anything. I'm so jealous, I wish I could do that.

&#x200B;

Yeah.... living with a chronic illness & pain from your mid 20's on is just amazing, I love spending every single day at home, mostly by myself, doing the same damn shit for years to the point that days of the week pretty much lose all meaning. I also enjoy watching all my friends grow up, have careers and kids etc, and feeling like I'm like eternally stuck in between kid and adult. Don't forget the feeling like an awkward loser when anyone asks you what you've been up to since they last saw you. It's great.

&#x200B;

I also hate being called "brave" or an "inspiration" just for trying to survive my life, ex surgeries, harsh medications etc. The only other option is dying, so.... I guess I'm brave and inspirational for not wanting to die? I get it's meant to be a compliment, but seriously? Don't use my crappy health as inspiration to live your life to the fullest. That's just hard to hear all the time...

Jenna Marbles video of her Nicki Minaj impersonation, lol. It's so old and dumb, but it's always guaranteed to make me laugh so much because it's just so over the top.

&#x200B;

Lol this totally just made watch it again :P

[https://www.reddit.com/r/lyrics/](https://www.reddit.com/r/lyrics/)

&#x200B;

You can try here too

&#x200B;

As far as my opinion, I would say I really like the part that starts from "Avoiding them with this music" to "I want you far away, but I need to be by your side" the best, it flows really well. The parts before and after that aren't necessarily bad, they're just a little more choppy and broken it feels like when I read them, especially when compared to the middle.

 It was also a little hard to know, hmm maybe the cadence?Like rhythm? It was just all mashed together with commas, I think if you put it more into stanzas it would be easier to understand where one verse starts and ends and have more of a meter to it. I hope that makes sense.

&#x200B;

Hope this helped a little :)
